    },
    {
      "path": "docs/RESULTS.md",
      "line": 35,
      "text": "Each successful row selects the lowest recorded peak after repair, using the latest evaluation to break ties. Unsolved rows use the latest baseline documented in that row. The s2 row uses the larger AdamW workload. Memory values are **decimal GB = bytes / 1,000,000,000**."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/RESULTS.md",
      "line": 49,
      "text": "The selected s1 run ties the earlier lowest successful after-peak byte count (14,297,204,736), so the latest-on-tie rule selects the later October 30 partial check at revision 5a013bf3. Its candidate and checkpoint-transformed reference each completed 20 updates; formal numerical acceptance covers only their first five backward scalars. Pairing checks matched. Selecting this one qualifying result does not turn the partial check into a complete evaluation."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/RESULTS.md",
      "line": 51,
      "text": "The selected s8 run at revision c21cf546 has the same lowest successful after-peak byte count (121,791,488) as the previous selected run. The latest-on-tie rule selects R17; its 20 recorded losses are identical, but full workload pairing remains unknown and this adds no distinct historical success."
