      "text": "Historical coverage combines successes from different evaluations; it is not a single-run success rate. The successful s4 peak ties its earlier best, so the selection rule chooses the latest run. The public gallery contains four successful cases and two failures. Its s3 card now uses the separate browser demonstration, and its s4 card uses the selected October 29 run; this does not change the campaign-only historical table. The separate precision-policy and HF tests added no successful gallery cards."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/RESULTS.md",
      "line": 146,
      "text": "The latest complete October 30 evaluation met three of nine memory targets, below the requirement of six. Its first saved diagnosis rounds had 5 valid correct first causes and 5 ready diagnoses; five final diagnoses were valid and three remained ready at the stopping point. In the earlier R10 evaluation, all nine ran and none met its repair target; that historical row is retained above. s5 and nanoGPT retain unverified reference causes and stay in the denominator. R7, where s4 met its target, is retained as historical evidence. A valid cause or a statically accepted edit does not establish a usable repair. The two extra s2 precision-policy tests and HF Trainer repair did not pass, and no successful memory-versus-speed comparison was produced."
